                <pb facs="0749" n="743" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg743"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.48/2035: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the
                        United Kingdom (Winant)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-02-26T00:00:00-04:00">February 26,
                            1942—midnight.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>860. Your 845, February 22, midnight. The American Government will be glad to
                    associate itself with the British Government in the plans for the relief of
                    Greece as outlined in Mr. Eden’s letter.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
